    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/73dfe8f6-b808-44b4-a512-64714c49dcea-9894867.PNG\" style=\"width: 304px; height: 250px;\" /><br />&nbsp;<p>Following are the correct versions of the two incorrect statements:<br />(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math> for electrolyte <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is cannot be obtained by extrapolation as the curve for A is diverging away from the y-axis</p><p>(C)&nbsp;At infinite dilution, value of degree of dissociation approaches one for electrolyte B</p>",
